    "summary": "Garden ’82 bursts with scorching Shakedown, epic Scarlet > Fire and Brent’s vibrant keys",
    "review": "What unfolds at Madison Square Garden on September 20, 1982 is a high‑octane snapshot of the Dead in full swing. The set opens with an electric “Shakedown Street” that never lets up, rolling straight into a blistering first set packed with tight renditions of “Dupree’s Diamond Blues,” “Row Jimmy,” and a seamless “Throwing Stones → Keep Your Day Job” finish. The second set is the real centerpiece: a 12‑minute, tightly knit “Scarlet Begonias > Fire on the Mountain” that showcases Jerry’s soaring leads and Brent’s playful keyboards, followed by a monster “Terrapin Station” jam and the legendary “Spanish Jam → Truckin’ → The Other One → Stella Blue → Sugar Magnolia” sequence that keeps the crowd in a perpetual groove. The encore’s “Touch of Grey” caps a night where every transition feels intentional and every solo feels inspired.\n\nAcross the board the band is locked in – Jerry’s tone is crystal‑clear, Phil lays down a solid low‑end (even opening the riff to “The Other One” on a four‑string), Brent’s keyboard work adds both texture and humor, and Bill & Mickey keep the rhythm tight yet fluid. The energy never wanes, making this Garden run one of ’82’s most memorable entries in the Dead canon.",
